---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Kleep AI Project - Ryan Darius Lim">
    <div class="ux-projects" style="padding-top: 80px;">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="project-card">
                <div class="project-header">
                    <div class="project-title-row">
                        <img src="/kleep_logo.png" alt="Kleep logo" class="project-logo">
                        <h3 class="project-title">Startup's Website + Tailored App UIUX for Clients</h3>
                    </div>
                    <p class="project-role">Founders' Associate (Product & Operations)</p>
                    <p class="project-dates">Jan 2025 – Jun 2025 | NOC Paris, France</p>
                </div>

                <div class="project-content">
                    <div class="content-section">
                        <h4 class="content-section-title">Startup Overview</h4>
                        <p>
                            Kleep is an AI-powered size recommendation tool that integrates with fashion e-commerce websites 
                            as a subscribable add-on. The application helps customers find their perfect size through an 
                            interactive questionnaire or by taking two snapshots, effectively reducing return rates and 
                            increasing conversion rates for fashion retailers.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="content-section">
                        <h4 class="content-section-title">Website Responsibilities</h4>
                        <ul class="simple-list">
                            <li>Completely revamped the entire website via Framer with an enhanced content management system</li>
                            <li>Added carousel animations and interactive scroll animations</li>
                            <li>Embedded typeform + calendly to allow interested parties to 'book a demo' increasing the startup's own conversion and sales rate</li>
                            <li>Designed backdrops and stunning visuals matching the theme of the startup</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div style="margin: 20px 0;">
                        <a href="https://kleep.ai/" target="_blank" 
                           style="display: inline-block; background: #0366d6; color: white; padding: 12px 28px; 
                                  border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.05rem; 
                                  transition: background 0.2s;">
                            🚀 Launch the Kleep website
                        </a>
                    </div>

                    <div class="content-section">
                        <h4 class="content-section-title">App UX Responsibilities</h4>
                        <ul class="simple-list">
                            <li>Designed and customized app interfaces in Figma to match each client's brand identity, ensuring seamless integration with their website theme and user flow</li>
                            <li>Conducted multiple rounds of design iterations (typically 3-5 rounds) based on client feedback to achieve perfect visual and functional alignment</li>
                            <li>Implemented Google Analytics to track user behavior, identify drop-off points, and make data-driven improvements to the product flow</li>
                            <li>Successfully onboarded clients and integrated the Kleep app into their Shopify stores with full technical support</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <div class="project-image">
                        <img src="/kleep_uiux.png" alt="Kleep Figma design showing size recommendation interface">
                    </div>

                    <div class="content-section">
                        <h4 class="content-section-title">UX Problem & Solution</h4>
                        <p><strong>Challenge:</strong> Clients were worried about UI integration of the Kleep app into their websites + Analytics revealed users were dropping off during the questionnaire phase.</p>
                        
                        <p style="margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 10px;"><strong>My Approach:</strong></p>
                        <ul class="simple-list">
                            <li>Facilitated an efficient feedback loop with clients to make quick changes to Figma markups before deployment</li>
                            <li>Set up detailed Google Analytics event tracking to monitor each step of the user journey</li>
                            <li>Analyzed user session data to understand behavioral patterns and identify friction points</li>
                            <li>Identified that the questionnaire was too lengthy and questions lacked clarity</li>
                        </ul>
                        
                        <p style="margin-top: 25px; margin-bottom: 10px;"><strong>Solutions Implemented:</strong></p>
                        <ul class="simple-list">
                            <li>Redesigned questionnaire flow to be more progressive and less overwhelming</li>
                            <li>Simplified question wording and added visual aids (icons, images) for better comprehension</li>
                            <li>Recommended progress indicator to set user expectations and reduce perceived effort</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <div class="tools">
                        <span class="tool-tag">Figma</span>
                        <span class="tool-tag">Google Analytics 4</span>
                        <span class="tool-tag">Looker</span>
                        <span class="tool-tag">Shopify</span>
                        <span class="tool-tag">HTML/CSS/JS</span>
                    </div>

                    <div style="margin-top: 40px; padding-top: 30px; border-top: 2px solid #e1e4e8;">
                        <a href="/projects" style="color: #0366d6; font-weight: 600;">← Back to All Projects</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>
